        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3125441720\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27003\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003\">#27003</a> by <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Elchi3/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Elchi3\">@Elchi3</a> ran the BCD Collector for Chrome 135 beta but it seems to have set the Android support to false for any new entries but I see no reason for this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Some of these have been corrected manually (e.g. in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3125441720\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27003\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27003\">#27003</a>) but these have not.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Elchi3/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Elchi3\">@Elchi3</a> do you know why this was? Should I raise an issue for this? I don't see the same for the latest Chrome 144 beta nor, 134/136 either side of this bad one. So maybe a one off issue?</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">To be honest I have not tested these all, but I see no reason they were set to unsupported since, unless there is an exceptional reason, most changes to Chrome are also supported in Chrome Android and there are no reasons for these.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28660",
            "title": "Fix Android support for Chrome 135 beta APIs",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-13T16:08:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-13T16:05:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari 26.2 supports request-close but still marked as Tech Preview only</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The middle dialog here works:<br>\n<a href=\"https://codepen.io/web-dot-dev/pen/NPNVWPa\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codepen.io/web-dot-dev/pen/NPNVWPa</a></p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also noted here: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/17640/webkit-features-for-safari-26-2/#:~:text=close%2C%20and-,request%2Dclose,-.%20And%20for%20any\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/17640/webkit-features-for-safari-26-2/#:~:text=close%2C%20and-,request%2Dclose,-.%20And%20for%20any</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28659",
            "title": "Safari 26.2 supports request-close",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-13T15:44:33.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-13T15:35:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Correct erroneous LargestContentfulPaint data I spotted:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Safari and Firefox do not support <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code></li>\n<li>Safari DOES support cross-origin render times.</li>\n<li>Chrome does support <code class=\"notranslate\">paintTime</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> but behind a flag (unflagging in Chrome 145!)</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari does support cross-origin lcp render time but not <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> (tested on <a href=\"https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/lcp-cross-origin/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/lcp-cross-origin/</a>)<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198292-e3e64c66-0f96-4be1-97ce-351922bddcdf.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..jvTGtrjf9Hw2ZkeSEQESz8ssDOp5pRpHBKVfzE6HwGo\"><img width=\"1583\" height=\"810\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198292-e3e64c66-0f96-4be1-97ce-351922bddcdf.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..jvTGtrjf9Hw2ZkeSEQESz8ssDOp5pRpHBKVfzE6HwGo\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 810px;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Firefox gives null for <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code>:</strong></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198467-50acd617-cf85-4629-926a-607fbad2a6c9.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..sUZLbSGNSA18QwGdqk6G66iqS9L_r0cdT9sUs1A3GeA\"><img width=\"1481\" height=\"836\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198467-50acd617-cf85-4629-926a-607fbad2a6c9.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..sUZLbSGNSA18QwGdqk6G66iqS9L_r0cdT9sUs1A3GeA\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 836px;\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Chrome 134 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">paintTime</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">presentationTime</code> when experimental web platform features are turned on:</strong></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198260-3a01c5c9-b8d3-4375-843c-1c8de9e90d9f.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..dgUVrSM6qc4eASUlnHHPozyKHXB7otZU4IsA0L9YqBI\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1162\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/526198260-3a01c5c9-b8d3-4375-843c-1c8de9e90d9f.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..dgUVrSM6qc4eASUlnHHPozyKHXB7otZU4IsA0L9YqBI\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1162px;\"></a>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28658",
            "title": "Misc LargestContentfulPaint updates",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-13T15:11:58.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-13T15:11:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox 147 adds support for the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/counter-increment\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">counter-*</code></a> and <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/quotes\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">quotes</code></a> properties on the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/::marker\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">::marker</code></a> pseudo-element. See <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2000404\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2000404</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a separate data point for <code class=\"notranslate\">counter-*</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">quotes</code>, as I thought some browsers may conceivably add support separately, and they feel like different concerns.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have created a test case at <a href=\"https://codepen.io/Chris-Mills/pen/yyOGdGJ?editors=1100\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://codepen.io/Chris-Mills/pen/yyOGdGJ?editors=1100</a>. In testing, I found that the features:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Work in Firefox 147, but not 146</li>\n<li>Don't work in Chrome Canary or Safari technology preview.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28625",
            "title": "Firefox 147 supports `counter-*` and `quotes` properties on `::marker`",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-10T12:00:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-09T16:43:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/782446?u=b04ff20ddafb41870583859554c1e7c3180adca3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Added implementation URLs for Bun, Chrome and Node.js support.</p>",
